subproblems.statement:
Let N ∈ ℕ, ℝᴺ := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) with its Borel σ-algebra, μ a measure on ℝᴺ, M ⊆ ℝᴺ a measurable set, U ⊆ ℝᴺ open and F : ℝᴺ → ℝᴺ continuous on M. Assume:
(P) μ(M ∩ O) > 0 for every y ∈ M and every open O ⊆ ℝᴺ with y ∈ O;
(L) for every y ∈ M and every open O ∋ y there is ρ > 0 with B̄(y, ρ) ⊆ O and M ∩ B̄(y, ρ) compact;
(T) for every Y : ℝᴺ → ℝᴺ of class C² with compact support, tsupport Y ⊆ U and M ∩ tsupport Y compact, the function y ↦ ⟨Y(y), F(y)⟩ is μ-integrable on M and ∫_M ⟨Y(y), F(y)⟩ dμ(y) = 0.
Then F(y) = 0 for every y ∈ M ∩ U.
